const IDX=[{"title": "Renown", "url": "rules-renown.html", "text": "Renown\nd10 | Focused 10+ | Parry 8+ | Heal 8+ | src defaults\n A turn-based strategy game of empire building, diplomacy, and domain mastery.\n"}, {"title": "Introduction", "url": "rules-introduction.html", "text": "Introduction\nWithin the Realm, Empires expand, specialize, confer, and when diplomacy fails\u2014battle. You will lead your humble Province to greatness. Charter new Settlements, build your economy, and negotiate your way to victory. Will your religion dominate the Realm? Will your economy grow until your wealth is undeniable? Can you build a world wonder? Can you extort your way to victory? Pick your Faction, command your Domain, and pursue your Craft in this political grand strategy, where every action you attempt can be endorsed or condemned by your allies and other players.\nGame Synopsis\nRenown is a turn-based political strategy game for 1\u20137 players (3+ preferred) set in a medieval world of competing lords. Each player controls a growing empire \u2014 settlements, armies, and holdings \u2014 but the game\u2019s central tension isn\u2019t military. It\u2019s political.\nEvery action you want to take has to survive a vote. When you move your army, build a road, or sabotage a rival, every other player at the table gets to spend political influence to support or bury it. The strength of your relationships, the alliances you\u2019ve built, and the favors you\u2019re owed determine whether your plans succeed \u2014 not just your"}, {"title": "Reading These Rules", "url": "rules-reading-these-rules.html", "text": "Reading These Rules\nA few conventions make every rule in this book read the same way:\n\nmay marks something optional. If a rule doesn&#x27;t say may, it&#x27;s mandatory.\ncan&#x27;t and doesn&#x27;t are hard stops, and always win over a may or a must (see Core Principle 2).\nEffects are written by when they apply: While X is always on; When X / At X happens once, at that moment; an action&#x27;s Cost / Effect / Endorsed happens when you take the action.\nChoose one: marks a set of options from which you pick exactly one.\nItalic text is reminder, example, or strategy \u2014 it explains the rule but never changes it; the plain-text rule governs.\nCapitalized terms (Army, Envoy, Standing, Holding, Treaty\u2026) are defined terms \u2014 each section closes with a glossary of the terms it introduces, and the Index at the back lists every term with its page numbers.\n\nGlossary \u00b7 Reading the RulesTermDefinitionNatural rollThe number on the die before any modifiers. Modifiers never change what counts as &#x27;natural&#x27;.FocusedA natural 10, before modifiers.PerformWhen you Perform an action, immediately do the description of the action. Pay the action&#x27;s normal Cost.ResolveAttempt to Perform an action."}, {"title": "Core Principles", "url": "rules-core-principles.html", "text": "Core Principles\n\nGranted Power Any mechanic not explicitly described doesn&#x27;t function.\n\n\nSpecific over general. A more specific rule overrides a general one.\n\n2.1 Example: Inquisitorial Palace \u2265 Established Cunning &gt; general Cunning rule.\n2.2 When two effects conflict, the one that says can&#x27;t (or doesn&#x27;t) takes precedence over one that says you may or must.\n\n\n\nPublic information. All information is public: resources, Domains, Treaties, Armies, Holdings, and Garrisons are known to all players.\n\n\nOnce per turn, same target. A once-per-turn effect can&#x27;t be used on the same target twice in a turn.\n\n\nOne effect per Holding. A Holding has a single effect, active while the Holding is active.\n\n\nDamaged means inactive. A Damaged Holding or Infrastructure has no effect.\n\n\nTimer 0 resolves immediately. Any timer whose initial value is 0 or less resolves at once.\n\n\nDo as much as possible. Follow as much of an effect as you can; ignore any part you can&#x27;t carry out.\n\n\nDice.\n\n9.1 If a Roll is modified beyond 10+, it automatically fails.\n9.2 You can&#x27;t re-roll a re-roll, and you can&#x27;t re-roll a successful roll.\n9.3 Effects that occur on a 1 or 10 occur on unmod"}, {"title": "The Turn", "url": "rules-the-turn.html", "text": "The Turn\nEach turn runs through five phases in order, then passes the Host and repeats:\n\nEmpire Phase \u2014 start of turn: activate Standing effects, apply the Season, increment timers, resolve Bandit Mechanics, gain Influence &amp; Envoys, collect income, and pay upkeep.\nCouncil Phase \u2014 a Council vote on a Domain; each player then performs one action of that Domain.\nEnvoy Phase \u2014 send all Envoys, a Forum, vote on every Envoy, then resolve them all (Diplomacy \u2192 Prowess \u2192 Cunning \u2192 Piety \u2192 Industry).\nBattle Phase \u2014 Skirmishes, Sieges, and Battles resolve.\nRest Phase \u2014 cleanup, change Season, score Renown, spend one Domain Point, pass the Host.\n\nThe Host. Each turn except Spring, one player is the Host. The starting player is always the player directly clockwise from the Host token, including in Spring. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (except in Spring). The Host runs most of that Empire Phase&#x27;s administration: collecting and distributing Trade Income, resolving Bandit Mechanics, and breaking ties (Council vote, Bandit targeting, and anything not otherwise resolvable). The Host Card carries the step-by-step detail.\nTimers\nMany actions set a Timer to a number of turns. Each"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "rules-seasons.html", "text": "Seasons\nThe Realm cycles through four Seasons. The current Season&#x27;s effect is applied during the Empire Phase, and the Rest Phase advances the Season by one.\nSeasonNameEffectWinterFreezingAll Armies gain Speed -1; Sieges do not increment. Tax income collected.SpringPlantingNo Host, Bandit actions, Trade Income, Council Phase, or Diplomacy Actions. Players don&#x27;t gain Influence tokens. Bandit Camps Spawn.SummerCampaigningAll Armies gain Speed +2FallHarvestHusbandry Income is doubled."}, {"title": "Table Setup", "url": "rules-table-setup.html", "text": "Table Setup\n\nDomain Board: set Renown to 1, set each player&#x27;s Standing in each Domain to 1, set Season to Summer, and set Public Order to 0.\nGive the Host Card to the player who wants to Host first. If more than one, roll off.\nHex Map.\nTactic Decks, Equipment &amp; Retinue Cards, Holding Tiles, Bandit Camps, and the various tokens.\n"}, {"title": "Player Setup", "url": "rules-player-setup.html", "text": "Player Setup\n\nPick a Faction Card (optional for new players).\nEmpire Tableau.\nCollect 1 Town and 1 Hamlet. Take turns placing Towns, starting with the Starting player. Then each player may place their Hamlet Range 2 from their Town. Then place Outlaw Country Range 2 from their Town, but not adjacent to their Hamlet.\nCollect 10000 Gold, 2 Influence Tokens, and 1 Envoy.\nYou don&#x27;t begin the game with any Armies.\nFor the first turn, begin at the Council Phase instead of the Empire Phase.\n"}, {"title": "Action Mechanics", "url": "rules-action-mechanics.html", "text": "Action Mechanics\nSending an Envoy\nEnvoys are the currency of actions: to perform an action you send an Envoy during the Envoy Phase. Sending costs 1 Envoy, and you must be able to pay the action&#x27;s cost before you send it. Declare the Domain but not the action \u2014 &quot;I&#x27;d like to send a [Domain] Envoy.&quot; Envoys never target: you choose the action, and its target, only after the Envoy passes, so no one knows exactly what will happen until then.\nResolving an Envoy\nYour Envoy begins with Authority equal to your innate Authority in its Domain \u2014 Untested 1, Rising 2, Established 3, Sovereign 4 \u2014 plus any automatic Authority \u00b1X modifiers. (These come from your Holdings, Infrastructure, and faction, and apply on their own; you never spend Influence for them.) Diplomacy has no Standing; a Diplomacy Envoy begins with Authority set by the Era (Founding 1, Ascension 2, Eminence 3, Zenith 4).\nThen, clockwise from the starting player and skipping the sender, every other player may respond, with no talking during the vote:\n\nSupport X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to raise the Envoy&#x27;s net Authority.\nOppose X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to lower it.\nAbstain \u2014 spend nothing.\n\nYou sp"}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "rules-influence.html", "text": "Influence\nEach turn, gain Influence from the following sources:\nSourceInfluence ChangeNotesEra+1/+2/+3/+4Based on the Current EraTrading Partners+1Per Trading Partner.Alliances+1Per Alliance Member.Infrastructure tier completed+1Per Infrastructure tier fully completed.Cunning Standing+1per unlocked Cunning Standing.Fully Mustered Army+1Per active Army of 25 Retinues.Condemned Envoy last turn-1Per Condemned Envoy last turn.At War-3While at War.Monuments &amp; Wonders+1Per active Monument or Wonder.Other sources+XFrom other effects like Holdings.\n"}, {"title": "Prowess Actions", "url": "rules-prowess-actions.html", "text": "Prowess Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedMoveNone\u2014Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege. \u2014 Unless the move action was Endorsed, an Army may be the target of only one Move action per turn.; While an Army&#x27;s Battle or Siege Timer is active, it can&#x27;t be the target of actions.; When an Army performs the Battle action, it gains Seize the Initiative in that Battle&#x27;s first Skirmish.Perform another Move action (same or a different Army).Declare WarNoneRising ProwessChoose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you. \u2014 If you are in a Military Alliance, then at the start of your next turn every member Declares War on the target and sends 1 fewer Envoy that turn.Perform a Move action.PillageNoneRising ProwessChoose an army you control within Reach of an"}, {"title": "Cunning Actions", "url": "rules-cunning-actions.html", "text": "Cunning Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedIntercept Caravan2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income. \u2014 This affects only a single turn&#x27;s trade income; normal income resumes afterward.Extort 2000.Foster Rebellion2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country. \u2014 If that player&#x27;s Outlaw Country has no room, expand it by one Territory and spawn there instead.Extort 2000.Raze2000 gold\u2014Choose another player&#x27;s Settlement, then choose one active Holding, active Infrastructure, or active Build Timer in it: that target becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. A Damaged Build Timer doesn&#x27;t increment until Repaired. \u2014 A Wonder has Immune Razed and can&#x27;t be targeted.Extort 2000.Destabilize2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. In the next Winter phase, during the Extort step, Extort one settlement&#x27;s tax income. Each settlement can only be Destabilized once per Winter. \u2014 If multiple players extort the same player, the player with the highest Cunning value chooses which settlement(s) are extorted first. In the event of a "}, {"title": "Piety Actions", "url": "rules-piety-actions.html", "text": "Piety Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSpread TruthDoubt 1\u2014Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1.Recoup Doubt.Send MissionariesDoubt 1\u2014Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2.Recoup Doubt.TitheDoubt 1\u2014Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0).Recoup Doubt.ConvertDoubt 1\u2014Choose another player&#x27;s closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be -5 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture). \u2014 If the target&#x27;s Public Order rises to 1 or higher before the timer reaches 0, the Convert fails and the timer is removed.Recoup Doubt.Sacred WarDoubt 1Sovereign PietyDeclare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies. \u2014 While a Sacred War is active, neither player may Declare War on, Sign or End a Treaty with, Negotiate with, or De"}, {"title": "Industry Actions", "url": "rules-industry-actions.html", "text": "Industry Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedImprove2000 gold\u2014Choose one: Infrastructure \u2014 choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time; when it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your province. Or Expand a Settlement one tier into an adjacent Territory (Village to Town, Town to City, City to Metropolis), adding a Ward. \u2014 You must have at least one Infrastructure from the prior tier before building the next tier.; A Wonder is built in your capital and requires all other Infrastructure to be active when the Improve action is performed.; To upgrade to City or Metropolis you must meet that tier&#x27;s requirements; otherwise set Build Timer 1.Recoup 2000.Repair0 gold\u2014Choose a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Build Timer 2. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Holding tile from your Empire Tableau.Recoup 0.Build2000 gold\u2014Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Holding with one complete line of its Mastery Chain under your control (and meet its other requirements) and set a Buil"}, {"title": "Diplomacy Actions", "url": "rules-diplomacy-actions.html", "text": "Diplomacy Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSign TreatyNone\u2014Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance. \u2014 When acting on behalf of an Alliance, End Treaty requires all allies to agree.; A player can&#x27;t be in more than one Alliance.Faith +1.NegotiateNone\u2014Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding). \u2014 If a promise goes unfulfilled, the affected player may Declare War on the promiser.; Also used to resolve Demand Tribute and Siege surrenders.Faith +1.End TreatyNone\u2014Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn&#x27;t need to agree.Faith +1.\n\nRule: Diplomatic Mission\nIf your Diplomacy Envoy fails, you may send another Envoy in another Domain, resolved in the order it would be resolved alongside other envoys.\nGlossary \u00b7 Actio"}, {"title": "Domains & Standings", "url": "rules-domains-standings.html", "text": "Domains &amp; Standings\nDomain Standings\n \tDomains are the identity of your character in Renown. As you gain Renown each turn, you gain a Domain Point, which you may spend in any of the four Domains. Each Domain Point raises your Domain value by 1 in that Domain. When your Domain value reaches 3, you become Rising in that Domain \u2014 you may spend one extra Influence on another player&#x27;s Envoy of that Domain, and your Envoys gain Authority +1. This continues at a Domain value of 6 (Established) and again at 10 (Sovereign).\nEach Standing you gain in a Domain makes you harder to oppose there and lets you oppose others more easily with your Influence. You also gain a unique effect at each Standing that makes it easier to achieve that Domain&#x27;s objectives.\n Domain Identities &amp; Traits\nDomainUntestedRising (3)Established (6)Sovereign (10)Industry\u2014Trade Secrets: Perform endorsed Holding.Grand Architect: May have an additional City. Perform endorsed Improve.Titan of Industry: Your capital may be improved to a Metropolis. Perform endorsed Improve.Prowess\u2014Indomitable: Once per turn, if you have not sent a Personal Envoy, you may instead perform a Prowess action; send 1 fewer Envoy t"}, {"title": "Diplomacy & Treaties", "url": "rules-diplomacy-treaties.html", "text": "Diplomacy &amp; Treaties\nTreaties &amp; Alliances\nTreatySigned ViaEraEffectPeace TreatySign TreatyAnyEnds war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5.Trade AgreementSign TreatyAnyBegin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires bordering + active Dirt Road.Non-Aggression PactSign TreatyAnyNeither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5.Military AllianceSign TreatyEminenceMutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy).Defensive AllianceSign TreatyZenithMutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker.\n Alliance Rules:\nNew alliance members are added by unanimous agreement.A player cannot be in more than one alliance at a time.An alliance may remove a member via End Treaty if all others agree.\nVassalization\nTo vassalize a player:\n\nControl that player&#x27;s capital Settlement while the player has no other Settlements or Armies under their Control.\n\n\nAt the end of the Rest Phase, return every Settlement you Control that was chartered by that player to that player. You become their Suzerain, and they become your Vassal.\n"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "rules-settlements.html", "text": "Settlements\nSettlements are the primary vehicle of your Empire. They come in tiers: villages, towns, cities, and a capital Metropolis. Each tier provides tax income each turn, Settlement Wards that a Holding can fill, and a per-turn muster limit of Retinues. The values per tier are below:\nSettlementTaxMusterWardsReachBuildNotesHamlet00311Natural holdings only; exactly range 2 from capital; may always pursue Arable LandVillage10005122Town200010244City300025366Metropolis400050488Capital only, requires Sovereign Industry (Titan of Industry)\nSettlement Wards\nA Settlement contains 1 Settlement Ward for each of its tiers. A Village has 1 central hub, which all other Settlement Wards must be adjacent to (range 1); a Town has 2 Wards, a City has 3, and a Metropolis may have 4. The one exception is a Hamlet: it can hold only Husbandry Holdings, but contains 3 Settlement Wards.\nChartering Settlements\nWhen chartering a new Settlement, place it in your province, at least range 4 from all other Settlements and range 2 from any Outlaw Country. You can&#x27;t charter a Settlement on mountain or water Territory.\nSettlement Reach\nSettlements have a Reach value set by their tier, from 2 up to 8. Rea"}, {"title": "Infrastructure", "url": "rules-infrastructure.html", "text": "Infrastructure\n \tInfrastructure is the foundation of your Settlements. Each active Infrastructure provides an effect that applies to your entire empire and all its Settlements.\n \tExample: Wooden Walls protect all Settlements from Bandits and Raze actions, and a Cathedral raises your innate Faith by 2 each turn, regardless of how many Settlements you have.\n \tInfrastructure comes in 4 ascending tiers. Primitive Infrastructure builds the basic blocks of your empire. Developed Infrastructure expands and replaces some primitive Infrastructure. Sophisticated Infrastructure allows more powerful effects and helps unlock unique Monument Holdings.\n \tTo build any Infrastructure, you need at least one active Infrastructure of the tier below it \u2014 so Developed needs one Primitive, and Sophisticated needs one Developed (and therefore one Primitive). One Tier Primitive means any one Primitive Infrastructure. Some Infrastructure also names its own requirement on top of this: a Library needs a Town Hall, and a Cathedral needs a Capital City \u2014 so a Cathedral needs one Primitive, one Developed, and a Capital City.\n \tLast are world Wonders. Wonders are unique Infrastructure, each built once per game, o"}, {"title": "Territory & Terrain", "url": "rules-territory-terrain.html", "text": "Territory &amp; Terrain\nTerritory is the smallest unit of land. To move from one Territory to another, you move range 1. To be within a Territory is range 0; adjacent is range 1; next to is range 2.\nSpeed X \u2014 An Army&#x27;s movement range in Territories per Move action. Base Speed value of an army is Speed 3\n \tTerritories carry modifiers by hex type (grassland, forest, tundra, wetlands, water, mountain), and are uncontrolled, contested, or controlled. Territory begins uncontrolled. By chartering Settlements you Control Territories: each Settlement&#x27;s Reach X adds every Territory within that range to your province. If another player&#x27;s Settlement Reach reaches any Territory you Control, that Territory is contested.\n \tTo border another player, your Reach must be within or adjacent to their Territory.\nTerrainMap EffectRaw MaterialsBattle EffectGrassland\u2014Arable Land, ApiaryHill: An army on a Hill Seizes the Initiative every Skirmish.  Open Field: Ranged Weapons gain +1 to Strike.WetlandsSpeed -1 per Territory moved throughPeat Bog, ForestryMire: Gain Unwieldy and Immune Steady; -1 to Save.Tundragain StrainedQuarry, Salt WorksGain Strained.MountainsImpassableMine, QuarryImpassab"}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "rules-public-order.html", "text": "Public Order\nFaith and Doubt adjust your Public Order the moment they&#x27;re generated \u2014 each Faith raises it by 1, each Doubt lowers it by 1, applied immediately. Public Order is capped between -5 and 10, and your current band&#x27;s effects (below) are always active at your current value.\nFirst Doubt of the turn. Some effects (e.g. Reliquary Sanctum, Episcopal Court) reduce the first Doubt you gain each turn, from any source. Because Doubt now applies immediately, this is whichever Doubt lands first in the turn \u2014 usually your innate modifiers in the Empire Phase, but it can be an opponent&#x27;s action if that resolves first. Track whether you&#x27;ve taken Doubt yet this turn; the marker resets at the start of each Empire Phase, before innate modifiers apply.\nYour innate Public Order modifiers (below) are checked once each turn during the Empire Phase and applied like any other Faith/Doubt.\nPOStateEffect-5UprisingBandit Camp spawns in your Outlaw Country-4Recession-1000 Tax Income per Settlement-3AimlessSpeed -2-2Indecisive-1 Influence-1WaveringNo effect0NeutralNo effect1FocusedNo effect2Confident+1 Influence3MotivatedSpeed +14Economic BoomTax income +500 per settlement5EurekaM"}, {"title": "Treasury & Upkeep", "url": "rules-treasury-upkeep.html", "text": "Treasury &amp; Upkeep\nYour Treasury is the gold you Control. Each Empire Phase you gain your Revenue (tax, trade, and Holding income) and pay your Upkeep (Armies, Holdings, and Infrastructure); the net lands in your Treasury. Costs you pay during the turn come out of the same Treasury.\nHolding upkeep is fixed by Holding type: Monument 300, Power 200, Energy 0, all others 100. Holdings and Infrastructure only pay upkeep while active: none while being built, Damaged, or under repair.\nArmy upkeep = the sum of each Army&#x27;s cost (by Retinue type) \u2212 Upkeep modifiers. Army costs by Retinue type: Levy 1000, Man-at-Arms 2000, Sergeant 2000, Oathsworn 2000.\nTracking tip: keep three small piles \u2014 Treasury, Revenue, Upkeep. When you build something with income or upkeep, add it to the matching pile; when it&#x27;s damaged or an Army is disbanded, subtract it. Each turn it&#x27;s just Treasury + Revenue \u2212 Upkeep, with no recounting.\nInsolvency &amp; Bankruptcy\n&gt; This is an exception path \u2014 skip it until it happens.\nYou go Insolvent the moment your Treasury can&#x27;t cover a cost in full (at Upkeep, when paying for an action, or when an effect drains your gold). Pay what you can, then cu"}, {"title": "Trade & Income", "url": "rules-trade-income.html", "text": "Trade &amp; Income\nWho Can Trade &amp; Income\nWho can trade: a player needs active dirt road Infrastructure and a signed Trade Agreement to take part in trade.\nCraft X: Craft Holdings count toward how much income your Trade Agreements generate \u2014 any effect that grants Craft +X.\nTrade income: for each active Trade Agreement, both players gain gold equal to 100 \u00d7 the Host&#x27;s Craft X.\nWhen income flows:\n\nWhen you sign a Trade Agreement: the player who did not perform the Sign Treaty action gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host. Afterwards, both get trade income each turn either of them is Host.\nWhen you end a Trade Agreement: the player who ended it gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host, then trading ceases.\n\nRuleValueIncome per Craft100RequirementsPlayers must have active Dirt Road infrastructure, and a signed Trade AgreementNo-trade seasonSpringTax seasonWinter\nIncome Types\n\nTaxes: at the start of each Winter, gain tax income equal to your Settlement total, after modifiers.\nTrade: see above.\nHoldings: gain Holding effect income at the start of the income phase.\n\nGlossary \u00b7 Economy &amp; Public OrderTermDefinitionPublic OrderA track from -5 to 10, adjusted"}, {"title": "Armies", "url": "rules-armies.html", "text": "Armies\nArmies Overview\nArmies are collections of Retinues on the realm, and are the target of Move actions. An Army holds up to 25 Retinues and up to a single piece of equipment of each type (armor, weapon, shield, and Retinue).\n \tArmies cost upkeep, paid in the Empire Phase. Each Army costs its Retinue type&#x27;s cost; your Army upkeep is the total of all your Armies, minus any upkeep modifiers.\n \tExample: Net Upkeep = \u03a3(each Army&#x27;s cost by Retinue type) \u2212 Upkeep Modifiers.\nWhile an Army has been engaged in a Battle or Lay Siege action started by another player&#x27;s Army, neither Army can be the target of any actions until that Battle or Lay Siege resolves.\nMustering\nArmies are raised and reinforced with the Muster action (see Prowess Actions).\nDuring any Upkeep phase while an Army is within (range 0) a Settlement you Control, you may change that Army&#x27;s equipment to any unlocked equipment.\nRetinue types \u2014 cost, to-Strike, and base profile:\nRetinueCostTo StrikeEnduranceMoraleSpeedMax SizeKeywordLevy10006+27+325\u2014Man-at-Arms20005+36+325\u2014Sergeant20003+25+325\u2014Oathsworn20004+24+325\u2014\nBlocked Armies\nA Blocked Army has \u22121 Initiative in the first Skirmish and can&#x27;t perform"}, {"title": "Battle Phase", "url": "rules-battle-phase.html", "text": "Battle Phase\nBegin Battle\nBegin Skirmish\n\nDeclare Army \u2014 declare which Army will Skirmish (if more than one is adjacent to either Army in the Battle).\n\n\nChoose a Tactic and equipment \u2014 place a face-down Tactic, together with your equipment for this Skirmish if you have a choice (a Tiltyard, or a Bastard Sword&#x27;s 1H/2H profile); reveal both once the other player has too. A One-Shot weapon must be Equipped in the first Skirmish.\n\n\nResolve Tactic modifiers \u2014 after Tactics are revealed, apply the Initiative and any other modifiers from your Tactics and weapon profile.\n\nHow a Battle Resolves\nA Battle is fought as a series of Skirmishes, run through the steps below until one side is wiped out, Routs, or successfully Falls Back. Full keyword detail is in the glossary tables at the end of this section.\nBegin the Battle \u2014 Seize the Initiative\nDetermine who gains Seize the Initiative. Typically, the player who performed the Battle Action gains Seize the Initiative, but Terrain and the Ministry of Military Strategy can affect that. When a player gains Seize the Initiative, the player gains +1 Initiative in the first round of combat.\nThe Skirmish Steps\n\nForm the line. Each side places up t"}, {"title": "Siege Warfare", "url": "rules-siege-warfare.html", "text": "Siege Warfare\n\nWhen you Lay Siege during the Envoy Phase, track the relevant Siege Timer(s).\nWhen a Siege Timer reaches 0, resolve the Siege before the Rest Phase: negotiate, then Battle if needed, then capture or sack.\nFor the full sequence, see the steps below.\n\nSiege Timer\nA Siege Timer is the sum of the besieged Settlement&#x27;s defenses minus the attacker&#x27;s Siege effects, to a minimum of 1 (no maximum). Walls stack \u2014 Wooden Walls (+1) and Stone Walls (+2) both count.\nSourceTimerNoteSettlement Size+0 to +4settlement tier (Hamlet 0 \u2026 Metropolis 4)Wooden Walls+1Stone Walls+2Citadel+3Garrison+1Standing Army+1army at range 0 of the settlementAttacker effects\u2212 variesOrdinance Yard \u22121, Siege Camp \u22121, Siege Works \u22122\nBeginning a Siege\n\nEnd a Move action with your Army adjacent to another player&#x27;s Settlement you&#x27;re At War with.\n\n\nYour Army must stay there for the Siege Timer and can&#x27;t take other actions.\n\n\nIf you&#x27;re attacked while sieging and you Fall Back, the Siege is broken and the Siege Timer is removed from play.\n\n\nWhile a Settlement is besieged: it can&#x27;t count Holdings toward Craft X; its Armies gain Blocked except to sally forth; timers targeting th"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "rules-bandits.html", "text": "Bandits\nOutlaw Country\nOutlaw Country is a cluster of Territory in your starting Settlement region that you can&#x27;t Control. At the start of the game, demarcate 3 Territories in your starting region, each within range 1 of at least one other Outlaw Country Territory and at least range 2 from any Settlement.\nIf that&#x27;s not possible, place them range 2 from your capital Settlement.\nSpawning Bandit Camps\nAt the start of the Bandit Mechanics step in Spring: place a Bandit Camp of 5 Bandits (Retinues) in each player&#x27;s Outlaw Country.\nNote: if an Outlaw Country is chosen to receive another Bandit Camp but there&#x27;s no room to place one, instead each existing Bandit Camp grows according to the current Era.\nGrowing Bandit Camps\nA Bandit Camp becomes a Bandit Army when it reaches 25 Retinues.\nBandit Armaments by Era\nEraArmamentFoundingLevy: Cudgel + ClothAscensionLevy: Arming Sword, Targe Shield, &amp; Leather ArmorEminenceMan-at-Arms: Halberd + ChainmailZenithMan-at-Arms: Battle Axe + Full Plate\nBandit Growth by Era\nEraRetinues Gained per TurnFounding1Ascension2Eminence3Zenith4\nBandit Info\nBandits share the same Renown level as players. A Bandit&#x27;s Domain value is set by"}, {"title": "Holdings", "url": "rules-holdings.html", "text": "Holdings\nArmsHoldingDomainInfrastructure ReqMastery ChainEffectArmoryRising Industry\u2014Tannery, BlacksmithUnlock Wrought armor &amp; shield; Upkeep -500; Craft +1BlacksmithRising Industry\u2014FurnaceCraft +1; Unlocks Wrought WeaponsCarpentry\u2014\u2014ForestryBuild Timer \u22121; +500, Craft+1Court ArmouryEstablished Industry\u2014Gilded FoundryPlanishing: Your to-Save can&#x27;t be reduced beyond 10+. Upkeep -500; Tempered Armor &amp; Shield UnlockedFletchery\u2014\u2014CarpentryUnlocks Ranged Weapons; Upkeep -200ForgeEstablished Industry\u2014BlacksmithCraft +2; Unlocks Forged Tier WeaponsFurnace\u2014\u2014MineUnlocks Cast Weapons; +500Gilded FoundryEstablished Industry\u2014ArmoryUpkeep -500; Unlock Forged armor &amp; shield.JoineryRising Industry\u2014Carpentryunlocks Shields; Upkeep -500Master WorkshopEstablished Industry\u2014ForgeUpkeep -500; Craft +1; Add Serrated to WeaponsStable1 Rising\u2014Animal HusbandrySpeed +2, Natural; Unlocks Cavalry Spear (Still requires Tier Unlock)Tannery\u2014\u2014Animal Husbandry, JoineryNatural; Unlocks Cast armor &amp; shield. Upkeep -500; Craft +1TiltyardEstablished Prowess\u2014FletcheryArmies may be equipped with a Ranged and a Melee Weapon simultaneously; In addition, armies may equip two of the same 1H Melee Weapon t"}, {"title": "Melee Weapons", "url": "rules-melee-weapons.html", "text": "Melee Weapons\nWeaponTierAPInitKeywordsFarm ToolCrude0+0AwkwardCudgelCrude-1-12H, Unwieldy, AwkwardPitchforkCrude0+12H, Unwieldy, AwkwardDaggersCast0+12H, DeadlyShort SwordCast0+0SteadySpearCast-1+1UnwieldyArming SwordWrought-1+0SteadyPikeWrought-1+12H, Steady, Unwieldy, Deadly, AwkwardFlailWrought-1+0Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Cleave, AwkwardHalberdWrought-2+02H, UnwieldyBattle AxeWrought-3-12H, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Cleave, Negate ShieldedCavalry SpearWrought-2+1Steady, Unwieldy, Negate Riposte, AwkwardMorningstarForged-4-1Cleave, Destroy ShieldBastard SwordForged-2+0Steady2HBastardForged-2+02H, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, CleaveWar HammerForged-10-12H, Unwieldy, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Negate Riposte, Destroy ShieldLanceForged-5+1Steady, Unwieldy, Deadly, Unstoppable, Awkward, Negate Riposte, Destroy ShieldEstocTempered-3+0Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Riposte, Negate PlanishingPoleaxeTempered-5+02H, Steady, Cleave, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Negate Planishing"}, {"title": "Ranged Weapons", "url": "rules-ranged-weapons.html", "text": "Ranged Weapons\nRanged WeaponTierAPInitKeywordsHunting BowCrude0+22H, Unstoppable, Negate Riposte, AwkwardLongbowCast-1+22H, Unstoppable, Deadly, Negate Riposte, AwkwardThrowing AxeWrought-2+1Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Negate Riposte, Destroy Shield, One-Shot, AwkwardCrossbowForged-4+1Unwieldy, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Negate Riposte, AwkwardThrowing SpearTempered-5+1Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Negate Riposte, Destroy Shield, One-Shot, AwkwardArquebusGunpowder-6+22H, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Negate Riposte, Negate Planishing, Awkward"}, {"title": "Shields", "url": "rules-shields.html", "text": "Shields\nShieldTierSave BonusInitKeywordsNone\u2014+0+0\u2014Buckler ShieldCrude+1+0\u2014Targe ShieldCast+1+0Unwieldy, ShieldedKite ShieldWrought+1+0Steady, ShieldedTower ShieldForged+2+0Unwieldy, ShieldedHeater ShieldTempered+2+0Shielded, Immune Destroy Shield"}, {"title": "Armor", "url": "rules-armor.html", "text": "Armor\nArmorTierSaveKeywordsClothNone10+\u2014PaddedCrude8+\u2014LeatherCast7+\u2014ChainmailWrought6+\u2014Full PlateForged5+\u2014Gothic PlateTempered4+\u2014\nGlossary \u00b7 Equipment TiersTermDefinitionCrudeCrude equipment tier. Weapons: Farm Tool, Cudgel, Pitchfork; Ranged: Hunting Bow; Armor: Padded; Shield: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry (armor &amp; shield).Crude WeaponsCrude-tier weapons: Farm Tool, Cudgel, Pitchfork, Hunting Bow.Crude ArmorCrude-tier armor: Padded. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry.Crude ShieldsCrude-tier shields: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry.CastCast equipment tier. Weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spear; Ranged: Longbow; Armor: Leather; Shield: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery (armor &amp; shield), Furnace (weapons).Cast WeaponsCast-tier weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spear, Longbow. Unlocked by: Furnace.Cast ArmorCast-tier armor: Leather. Unlocked by: Tannery.Cast ShieldsCast-tier shields: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery.WroughtWrought equipment tier. Weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear; Ranged: Throwing Axe; Armor: Chainmail; Shield: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Blacksmith (weapons), Armory (armor &amp; shield).Wrought Weapo"}, {"title": "Factions", "url": "rules-factions.html", "text": "Factions\nFactionFeelDifficultyStrengthMechanicSiege SpecialistOffensive, ArrogantLowMediumYou begin the game with a Siege Works (no Ward, Natural). When a player builds a Citadel, you must Siege it as an Edict.HorsemastersFastLowMediumYou begin the game with a Stable (no Ward, Natural).Friends in Low PlacesScrappyLowLowYou begin the game with a Smuggler&#x27;s Nook (no Ward, Natural). Each turn, you may control one Bandit Camp outside your Territory. When a Bandit Camp is generated, you may place it in your Outlaw Country instead.The MonarchSovereign VoiceLowMediumEach turn, you choose every Council Envoy&#x27;s Domain. You abstain every Personal Envoy.Sea LanesPirate LifeLowMediumOther players can&#x27;t perform Intercept Caravan on you. You begin the game with a Shipyard (no Ward, Natural).Royal MarriageDiplomatic, InescapableLowMediumOnce per game, you may join an Alliance without unanimous consent, or form one with a player who isn&#x27;t in an Alliance. While in that Alliance, each member gains Faith +1 and +1 Influence per turn.Patient CourtPatient &amp; ReservedLowMediumYour unspent Influence isn&#x27;t discarded in the Rest Phase. While the Era is Zenith, you may spend up t"}, {"title": "Index", "url": "rules-index.html", "text": "Index\n"}, {"title": "Carpentry", "url": "type-arms.html#carpentry", "text": "Carpentry Arms **Build Timer \u22121**; +500, Craft+1 "}, {"title": "Fletchery", "url": "type-arms.html#fletchery", "text": "Fletchery Arms Unlocks **Ranged Weapons**; **Upkeep -200** "}, {"title": "Tannery", "url": "type-arms.html#tannery", "text": "Tannery Arms Natural; Unlocks **Cast** armor & shield. **Upkeep -500**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Joinery", "url": "type-arms.html#joinery", "text": "Joinery Arms unlocks **Shields**; **Upkeep -500** "}, {"title": "Furnace", "url": "type-arms.html#furnace", "text": "Furnace Arms Unlocks **Cast** Weapons; +500 "}, {"title": "Blacksmith", "url": "type-arms.html#blacksmith", "text": "Blacksmith Arms Craft +1; Unlocks **Wrought** Weapons "}, {"title": "Armory", "url": "type-arms.html#armory", "text": "Armory Arms Unlock **Wrought** armor & shield; **Upkeep -500**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Master Workshop", "url": "type-arms.html#master-workshop", "text": "Master Workshop Arms **Upkeep -500**; Craft +1; Add **Serrated** to Weapons "}, {"title": "Gilded Foundry", "url": "type-arms.html#gilded-foundry", "text": "Gilded Foundry Arms Upkeep -500; Unlock **Forged** armor & shield. "}, {"title": "Stable", "url": "type-arms.html#stable", "text": "Stable Arms **Speed +2**, Natural; Unlocks Cavalry Spear (Still requires Tier Unlock) "}, {"title": "Forge", "url": "type-arms.html#forge", "text": "Forge Arms Craft +2; Unlocks **Forged** Tier Weapons "}, {"title": "Tiltyard", "url": "type-arms.html#tiltyard", "text": "Tiltyard Arms Armies may be equipped with a Ranged and a Melee Weapon simultaneously; In addition, armies may equip two of the same 1H Melee Weapon to gain **Dual Wield**. "}, {"title": "Court Armoury", "url": "type-arms.html#court-armoury", "text": "Court Armoury Arms **Planishing**: Your to-Save can't be reduced beyond 10+. Upkeep -500; **Crafted** Armor & Shield Unlocked "}, {"title": "Butchery", "url": "type-logistics.html#butchery", "text": "Butchery Logistics Natural; +500; **Upkeep -500**; Craft+1 "}, {"title": "Smokehouse", "url": "type-logistics.html#smokehouse", "text": "Smokehouse Logistics Natural; Craft +2; **Upkeep -500** "}, {"title": "Caravanery", "url": "type-logistics.html#caravanery", "text": "Caravanery Logistics Natural; **Influence -2** to **Intercept Caravan actions** targeting your **settlements**; **Craft +2**; **Speed -2** to non-allied armies in your Province. "}, {"title": "Coliseum", "url": "type-logistics.html#coliseum", "text": "Coliseum Logistics **Faith +1** while at War; Unlocks **Man-at-Arms** for **Muster** "}, {"title": "Conditioning Field", "url": "type-logistics.html#conditioning-field", "text": "Conditioning Field Logistics **Faith +1** while not at War; Armies gain **Nimble** "}, {"title": "Grand Tournament", "url": "type-logistics.html#grand-tournament", "text": "Grand Tournament Logistics **Reach +1**, 3x/turn: exchange 500 gold for **1 Influence**; Armies gain **Riposte** & Improve Parry by +1. "}, {"title": "Charcoal Burner", "url": "type-logistics.html#charcoal-burner", "text": "Charcoal Burner Logistics Natural; +500 "}, {"title": "Kiln", "url": "type-logistics.html#kiln", "text": "Kiln Logistics Natural; +500 "}, {"title": "Levy Hall", "url": "type-logistics.html#levy-hall", "text": "Levy Hall Logistics Natural, Speed +1; **Upkeep -2000** while an army is range 0 of controlled settlement "}, {"title": "Siege Works", "url": "type-logistics.html#siege-works", "text": "Siege Works Logistics **Siege Timer \u22122**; Sieges Increment in **Winter** "}, {"title": "Siege Camp", "url": "type-logistics.html#siege-camp", "text": "Siege Camp Logistics **Siege Timer \u22121**; Armies gain **Immune Strained** during Lay Siege "}, {"title": "War College", "url": "type-logistics.html#war-college", "text": "War College Logistics Gain **+2 Influence** while At War; Unlocks **Sergeants** for Muster "}, {"title": "Masonry", "url": "type-works.html#masonry", "text": "Masonry Works No Upkeep on **Primitive Infrastructure**; **Build Timer \u22121** "}, {"title": "Workyard", "url": "type-works.html#workyard", "text": "Workyard Works Natural; **Doubt +1**, +1000 "}, {"title": "Storehouse", "url": "type-works.html#storehouse", "text": "Storehouse Works Natural; **Doubt +1**, +2000; **Build Timer \u22121** "}, {"title": "Census Hall", "url": "type-works.html#census-hall", "text": "Census Hall Works Natural; **Doubt +1**; +1000 "}, {"title": "Granary", "url": "type-works.html#granary", "text": "Granary Works Upkeep -500; Armies and Garrisons gain **Endurance** while Besieged "}, {"title": "Supply Depot", "url": "type-works.html#supply-depot", "text": "Supply Depot Works **Craft +2**; May **Muster** an Army in a Settlement under Siege and increment Muster Timers. "}, {"title": "Trade Guild", "url": "type-works.html#trade-guild", "text": "Trade Guild Works No Upkeep on **Developed Infrastructure**; **Build Timer \u22121** "}, {"title": "College of Engineering", "url": "type-works.html#college-of-engineering", "text": "College of Engineering Works No Upkeep on **Sophisticated Infrastructure**; **Build Timer \u22121** "}, {"title": "Burgages", "url": "type-works.html#burgages", "text": "Burgages Works Natural; **Faith +1** "}, {"title": "Citadel", "url": "type-works.html#citadel", "text": "Citadel Works **Siege Timer +3**, Controlled Settlements gain **Reach +1** "}, {"title": "Castle Hall", "url": "type-works.html#castle-hall", "text": "Castle Hall Works Doubt +1; Tax Income is Doubled. "}, {"title": "Alchemy", "url": "type-commerce.html#alchemy", "text": "Alchemy Commerce +500; Craft+2 "}, {"title": "Weavery", "url": "type-commerce.html#weavery", "text": "Weavery Commerce +1000; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Jewelry Foundry", "url": "type-commerce.html#jewelry-foundry", "text": "Jewelry Foundry Commerce +2000; **Influence +1** to Cunning actions targeting this player; Craft +5 "}, {"title": "Market Square", "url": "type-commerce.html#market-square", "text": "Market Square Commerce Craft +2; +500 "}, {"title": "Spice Merchant", "url": "type-commerce.html#spice-merchant", "text": "Spice Merchant Commerce Natural; +1000; Influence +1 to Cunning actions targeting you; Craft +4 "}, {"title": "Harbor", "url": "type-commerce.html#harbor", "text": "Harbor Commerce Craft +2; **Extort 500** per **player** without **Harbor** "}, {"title": "Merchant Quarter", "url": "type-commerce.html#merchant-quarter", "text": "Merchant Quarter Commerce +500; Trade Partners gain Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Money Lending", "url": "type-commerce.html#money-lending", "text": "Money Lending Commerce **Extort 1000**; May loan money to Trade Partners at 100 per 1000/turn interest(minimum 100); on Default: Perform **Demand Tribute** "}, {"title": "Shipyard", "url": "type-commerce.html#shipyard", "text": "Shipyard Commerce Craft +4; Water Territory treated as Grassland for movement "}, {"title": "Courtyard", "url": "type-commerce.html#courtyard", "text": "Courtyard Commerce Craft +1; **Faith +1** "}, {"title": "Artisan Workshop", "url": "type-commerce.html#artisan-workshop", "text": "Artisan Workshop Commerce +1000, **Faith +1** "}, {"title": "Court Artists", "url": "type-commerce.html#court-artists", "text": "Court Artists Commerce **Extort 500** twice; Targets of Extort from Court Artist gain **Faith +1** "}, {"title": "Emporium", "url": "type-commerce.html#emporium", "text": "Emporium Commerce +1000; Players who trade with you gain **Craft +3** "}, {"title": "Chandlery", "url": "type-devotion.html#chandlery", "text": "Chandlery Devotion Craft +1; **Influence \u22121** to Cunning actions targeting you "}, {"title": "Interrogation Chambers", "url": "type-devotion.html#interrogation-chambers", "text": "Interrogation Chambers Devotion Extort 500; Cunning actions targeting this player that cause Doubt are reduced by 1, to a minimum of 0. "}, {"title": "Abbey", "url": "type-devotion.html#abbey", "text": "Abbey Devotion Once/turn: **Influence +1** another player's Piety Envoy; **Influence \u22121** to Piety actions targeting you "}, {"title": "Reliquary", "url": "type-devotion.html#reliquary", "text": "Reliquary Devotion +500; First **Doubt** per turn reduced by 1 (min 0) "}, {"title": "Monastery", "url": "type-devotion.html#monastery", "text": "Monastery Devotion Reach +1; Other players can't Oppose your Piety Envoys "}, {"title": "Execution Dock", "url": "type-devotion.html#execution-dock", "text": "Execution Dock Devotion **Influence -2** to **Foster Rebellion actions** targeting your **settlements**; **Players** who **target** you or your **settlements** with **actions** that cause **doubt** gain **Doubt +1** "}, {"title": "Hospitaller", "url": "type-devotion.html#hospitaller", "text": "Hospitaller Devotion **Recover** improved by +1; Enduring: Successful Recovered rolls do not count towards the panic check threshold. "}, {"title": "Episcopal Court", "url": "type-devotion.html#episcopal-court", "text": "Episcopal Court Devotion **Faith +1**; Reduce the first instance of Doubt at start of turn by 1, min 0. "}, {"title": "Apothecary", "url": "type-devotion.html#apothecary", "text": "Apothecary Devotion +300; Gain Recover 8, or improve Recover by +1. "}, {"title": "Infirmary", "url": "type-devotion.html#infirmary", "text": "Infirmary Devotion +500; Improve Recover by +1 "}, {"title": "Pilgrimage Site", "url": "type-devotion.html#pilgrimage-site", "text": "Pilgrimage Site Devotion Natural; **Extort 500** every player without a Pilgrimage Site; **Doubt +1** to all other players without a Pilgrimage Site "}, {"title": "Inn", "url": "type-court.html#inn", "text": "Inn Court **Faith +1** for trading partners with Craft 3+; **Faith +1** "}, {"title": "Jester's Court", "url": "type-court.html#jester-s-court", "text": "Jester's Court Court First and second **Oppose** on an Envoy of yours each turn: reduce by 1 "}, {"title": "Bell Tower", "url": "type-court.html#bell-tower", "text": "Bell Tower Court **+1 Influence**/turn; **Influence +1** to envoys sent during the Council Phase. "}, {"title": "Embassy", "url": "type-court.html#embassy", "text": "Embassy Court Diplomacy Envoys cannot Fail; Other non-vassal players gain Faith +1 per Signed Treaty with you besides Peace. "}, {"title": "Academy", "url": "type-court.html#academy", "text": "Academy Court **Influence +1** to Council Envoys; gain +1 Influence per turn "}, {"title": "University", "url": "type-court.html#university", "text": "University Court May spend one additional **Influence** per Support or Oppose; +1 **Influence** per Domain you are Rising "}, {"title": "Courier Network", "url": "type-court.html#courier-network", "text": "Courier Network Court Once/turn before voting: **Influence \u22121** on Target Envoy; Once/turn: successfully Performed Personal Envoy can be Performed next turn; send 1 fewer Envoys next turn "}, {"title": "Toll House", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toll-house", "text": "Toll House Secrecy Natural, **Extort 2000** when non-Allied Army ends a Move action within Province; Once/turn: when an Army ends a Move action within Province: Perform a Diplomacy action targeting that army's player "}, {"title": "Secret Cellar", "url": "type-secrecy.html#secret-cellar", "text": "Secret Cellar Secrecy Natural; Passed Cunning envoys **Recoup 500 Gold**; Endorsed Cunning envoys **Recoup 1000 Gold** "}, {"title": "Smuggler's Nook", "url": "type-secrecy.html#smuggler-s-nook", "text": "Smuggler's Nook Secrecy gain Immune Uprising (Bandit Camp Spawn at -5PO); Bandit Camps in your Outlaw Country don't target you and instead target other players randomly. "}, {"title": "Syndicate Hub", "url": "type-secrecy.html#syndicate-hub", "text": "Syndicate Hub Secrecy Whenever a Bandit Camp within Province Extorts, you Extort the Bandit Camp for half the amount. "}, {"title": "Black Market", "url": "type-secrecy.html#black-market", "text": "Black Market Secrecy When another player **Extorts** gold from any source: **Extort 200** per 1000 (minimum 100) from that player at the end of that resolution. When another player **Recoups** gold from any source: **Extort 200** per 1000 (minimum 100) from that player at the end of that resolution. "}, {"title": "Forgery Workshop", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgery-workshop", "text": "Forgery Workshop Secrecy **Extort 300** anytime a player Opposes an Envoy of yours; Once/turn: attempt another Cunning Envoy targeting a different player if your Cunning Envoy Failed "}, {"title": "Toxicarium", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toxicarium", "text": "Toxicarium Secrecy Weapons gain **Poison**; Endorsed Cunning actions give an additional **Doubt +1** to Target "}, {"title": "Charnel House", "url": "type-secrecy.html#charnel-house", "text": "Charnel House Secrecy Indecisive, Aimless, & Recession effects are doubled for all players "}, {"title": "Beacon Towers", "url": "type-secrecy.html#beacon-towers", "text": "Beacon Towers Secrecy Natural; Once per turn, you may select an Army within Province and move it up to its modified Speed. Whenever a non-allied Army ends a Move action within Province, you may immediately perform a Move action "}, {"title": "Forgotten Catacombs", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgotten-catacombs", "text": "Forgotten Catacombs Secrecy Cunning actions targeting you can't be **Endorsed** "}, {"title": "Cipher Chamber", "url": "type-secrecy.html#cipher-chamber", "text": "Cipher Chamber Secrecy Once/turn: select an army you did not select last turn, that army gains Blocked. Once/turn: select any active **Timer** you did not select last turn; increase it by 2. "}, {"title": "Herb Garden", "url": "type-husbandry.html#herb-garden", "text": "Herb Garden Husbandry +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Animal Husbandry", "url": "type-husbandry.html#animal-husbandry", "text": "Animal Husbandry Husbandry **Natural**, Unlock **Crude** armor and shield. Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Saddlery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#saddlery", "text": "Saddlery Husbandry +500, **Natural**; Speed +1; Unlocks Lance (Still requires Tier Unlock) "}, {"title": "Vineyard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#vineyard", "text": "Vineyard Husbandry +500, **Natural**; +500 in **Fall** "}, {"title": "Orchard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#orchard", "text": "Orchard Husbandry +800, **Natural**; +200 in **Fall** "}, {"title": "Bakery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#bakery", "text": "Bakery Husbandry Natural; Faith +1; +500; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Meadery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#meadery", "text": "Meadery Husbandry Natural; **Faith +1**; **Speed +2** in **Winter** "}, {"title": "Winery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#winery", "text": "Winery Husbandry Natural; +800; Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Cidery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#cidery", "text": "Cidery Husbandry Natural; **Faith +1**; +800; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Mill", "url": "type-husbandry.html#mill", "text": "Mill Husbandry Natural; +500 "}, {"title": "Quarry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#quarry", "text": "Quarry Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Salt Works", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#salt-works", "text": "Salt Works Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Apiary", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#apiary", "text": "Apiary Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Peat Bog", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#peat-bog", "text": "Peat Bog Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Forestry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#forestry", "text": "Forestry Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Fishmongery", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#fishmongery", "text": "Fishmongery Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Mine", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#mine", "text": "Mine Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Arable Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#arable-land", "text": "Arable Land Raw Materials +500, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Common Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#common-land", "text": "Common Land Raw Materials +1000, **Natural**, **Doubt +1** "}, {"title": "Plague Pit", "url": "type-monument.html#plague-pit", "text": "Plague Pit Monument Cunning actions give an additional **Doubt +1** to Target; No longer affected by all Public Order effects (positive or negative). This player cannot be the target of a Convert action. "}, {"title": "Baggage Train", "url": "type-monument.html#baggage-train", "text": "Baggage Train Monument Natural; Armies do not pay Upkeep while in Province. Upkeep -2000 while not in Province. Once/turn, you may perform a Move action. "}, {"title": "Office of Works", "url": "type-monument.html#office-of-works", "text": "Office of Works Monument Natural; Settlements & allied armies inside them are not affected by 'Settlements being Besieged' restrictions. Siege Timer +2; Build Timer -3 "}, {"title": "Royal Pavilion", "url": "type-monument.html#royal-pavilion", "text": "Royal Pavilion Monument Armies gain **Immune Strained**, Improve Parry by +1; Gain +1 to Strike. Deadly, & Cleave also trigger Focused Strikes on a natural 8+. "}, {"title": "Imperial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#imperial-palace", "text": "Imperial Palace Monument Each Empire Phase, all non-allied players with a lower Prowess value gain Doubt +2. If your Envoy would fail, it passes instead. "}, {"title": "Artillery Park", "url": "type-monument.html#artillery-park", "text": "Artillery Park Monument Siege Timers ignore Wooden & Stone Walls. Unlocks Arquebus; Settlements you Siege can't Sally Forth. Siege Timer \u22121. "}, {"title": "Ministry of Military Strategy", "url": "type-monument.html#ministry-of-military-strategy", "text": "Ministry of Military Strategy Monument Always gains **Seize the Initiative**, and your opponent doesn't; max initiative is increased to 3; Gain Drilled. "}, {"title": "Thieves' Guild", "url": "type-monument.html#thieves-guild", "text": "Thieves' Guild Monument Whenever another player performs a Cunning action, you may recoup 1000 gold; **Extort half** of Trade Income from players who don't trade with you "}, {"title": "Senate Hall", "url": "type-monument.html#senate-hall", "text": "Senate Hall Monument **Faith +1**, gain **+1 Influence** per other player per Turn; Once/turn: Before players Support or Oppose, you may auto-**Condemn** an At War Envoy OR auto-**Endorse** an Ally's Envoy "}, {"title": "Papal Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#papal-palace", "text": "Papal Palace Monument You no longer pay cost for Piety Envoys. At the start of each turn, Tithe every other player with lower Piety, resolved in the Extort step. "}, {"title": "Inquisitorial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#inquisitorial-palace", "text": "Inquisitorial Palace Monument **Doubt 1**; Unlocks **Grand Vizier** which uses your **Piety Value** instead of **Cunning.**; All player actions that cause Doubt are increased by 1.  "}, {"title": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar", "url": "type-monument.html#preceptory-of-the-knight-s-templar", "text": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar Monument Armies gain **Righteous Fervour**: Automatically pass the first Panic Check of every Battle. Unlocks **Knight's Templar** for Muster "}, {"title": "Exalted Basilica", "url": "type-monument.html#exalted-basilica", "text": "Exalted Basilica Monument Your piety actions cause an additional **Doubt** or an additional **Faith**. Every turn, perform Endorsed Spread Truth. "}, {"title": "Manor House", "url": "type-monument.html#manor-house", "text": "Manor House Monument Natural; Gain +200 gold for each active natural Holding. "}, {"title": "Aristocratic Court", "url": "type-monument.html#aristocratic-court", "text": "Aristocratic Court Monument Each Empire Phase, Extort 1000 from each non-allied player with a lower Treasury. Your Vote counts as 2 votes toward Domain selection during the Council Phase. "}, {"title": "Studium Generale", "url": "type-monument.html#studium-generale", "text": "Studium Generale Monument +1 **Influence** per **Established** Standing; May gain one **Sovereign Domain** effect without spending the Domain Points "}, {"title": "Outlaw Rookery", "url": "type-monument.html#outlaw-rookery", "text": "Outlaw Rookery Monument Both Bandit Camps & you have Influence +1 on Cunning Envoys. Endorsed Foster Rebellion instead places Bandit Armies with 25 retinues. "}, {"title": "Advanced Blast Furnace", "url": "type-monument.html#advanced-blast-furnace", "text": "Advanced Blast Furnace Monument **Upkeep -1000**; **Crafted** Weapons Unlocked; Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Whispering Undercroft", "url": "type-monument.html#whispering-undercroft", "text": "Whispering Undercroft Monument You always vote last, after the Host. Once/turn when a player sends an Envoy: that player must declare the specific action & target they would Perform if the Envoy passes (including sub-Actions). If it passes, they must Perform that declared action at the declared target. "}, {"title": "Outrider Intercept Post", "url": "type-monument.html#outrider-intercept-post", "text": "Outrider Intercept Post Monument Natural; Every Skirmish, you may force your opponent to reveal their Tactic Card they selected before you select your own. "}, {"title": "Port Authority", "url": "type-monument.html#port-authority", "text": "Port Authority Monument Gain +100 per **Craft** "}, {"title": "Turn Sequence", "url": "turn-sequence.html", "text": "turn sequence empire council envoy battle rest phase order of play"}, {"title": "Dirt Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#dirt-roads", "text": "Dirt Roads infrastructure Can Trade; If you start a Move action within Province, gain Speed +1"}, {"title": "Hitching Post", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#hitching-post", "text": "Hitching Post infrastructure Craft +1"}, {"title": "Muster Field", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#muster-field", "text": "Muster Field infrastructure Can Muster"}, {"title": "Wooden Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#wooden-walls", "text": "Wooden Walls infrastructure **Influence -2** to **Raze actions** from players targeting your **settlements**. **Influence -1** to Bandit **Cunning actions** targeting your **settlements**."}, {"title": "Stone Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#stone-roads", "text": "Stone Roads infrastructure If you start a Move action within Province, gain additional Speed +1"}, {"title": "Town Hall", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#town-hall", "text": "Town Hall infrastructure +1 Influence per turn"}, {"title": "Bridges", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#bridges", "text": "Bridges infrastructure Armies cross Water Territory at full movement within Province; Stone Roads may be built over Water"}, {"title": "Garrison", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#garrison", "text": "Garrison infrastructure Local Armies form (10/15/25/50 by Settlement size). All Garrisons share Retinues & Equipment. Can't be targeted; may not Sally Forth while under Siege. Do not pay upkeep."}, {"title": "Stone Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#stone-walls", "text": "Stone Walls infrastructure **Influence -2** to **Destabilize actions** from players targeting your **settlements**. **Influence -1** to Bandit **Cunning actions** targeting your **settlements**."}, {"title": "Aqueducts", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#aqueducts", "text": "Aqueducts infrastructure Reach +1, Upkeep -500, Build Timer -1, +1 Influence"}, {"title": "Cathedral", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#cathedral", "text": "Cathedral infrastructure Faith +2"}, {"title": "Library", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#library", "text": "Library infrastructure Council Envoys you send are always Endorsed"}, {"title": "Colossus", "url": "wonders-ref.html#colossus", "text": "Colossus wonder You may **support** your own **prowess envoys** before other **players vote**. **Armies** move **Speed +2**, **Siege Timer -2**, & gain **Immune Blunder**."}, {"title": "The Grand Exchange", "url": "wonders-ref.html#the-grand-exchange", "text": "The Grand Exchange wonder Whenever you generate **Trade Income** you generate **thrice as much** for yourself."}, {"title": "The Eternal Sepulchre", "url": "wonders-ref.html#the-eternal-sepulchre", "text": "The Eternal Sepulchre wonder If your **Public Order** would ever be less than 5 set it to 5 instead. Public Order Modifiers are doubled. Your **Settlements** gain **Reach +2**."}, {"title": "High Chancery", "url": "wonders-ref.html#high-chancery", "text": "High Chancery wonder Once per turn: automatically **Condemn** or **Endorse** one Envoy Sent by any other player regardless of **Authority** after Influence has been spent."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Move Prowess action Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege."}, {"title": "Declare War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Declare War Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you."}, {"title": "Pillage", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Pillage Prowess action Choose an army you control within Reach of an at-war player's Settlement that is not under Siege. Until cancelled, while that army remains within Reach of that Settlement and does not Lay Siege, Battle, or March, it may Extort half of that Settlement's [holding & tax income] in the Empire Phase. A Settlement may be Pillaged once per Empire Phase. Pillage ends if [war ends / army leaves Reach / Settlement is besieged]."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Muster Prowess action Choose one: Raise \u2014 if you have fewer Armies than your Era allows, place a new Army; or Reinforce \u2014 choose an Army you control. The Army must be within range 2 of a Settlement you Control with an active Muster Field, and at least range 2 from any non-allied Army unless it is within (range 0) a Settlement you Control. Choose how many Retinues to recruit (an Army can't exceed 25) and set a Muster Timer equal to that number \u00f7 your combined muster limit, rounded up. Each turn the Muster Timer counts down, the Army gains Retinues up to your combined muster limit and you begin paying their upkeep. You may change the Army's Retinue type and equipment."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Demand Tribute Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP with, then negotiate terms. If the target agrees, sign a NAP or Alliance (the target picks among the offered terms). If the target refuses, or later fails to meet the terms, immediately Declare War on them."}, {"title": "Intercept Caravan", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Intercept Caravan Cunning action Choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income."}, {"title": "Foster Rebellion", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Foster Rebellion Cunning action Choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country."}, {"title": "Raze", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Raze Cunning action Choose another player's Settlement, then choose one active Holding, active Infrastructure, or active Build Timer in it: that target becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. A Damaged Build Timer doesn't increment until Repaired."}, {"title": "Destabilize", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Destabilize Cunning action Choose a player. In the next Winter phase, during the Extort step, Extort one settlement's tax income. Each settlement can only be Destabilized once per Winter."}, {"title": "Sabotage", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sabotage Cunning action Choose an army, that army gains Blocked."}, {"title": "Spread Truth", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Spread Truth Piety action Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1."}, {"title": "Send Missionaries", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Send Missionaries Piety action Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2."}, {"title": "Tithe", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Tithe Piety action Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0)."}, {"title": "Convert", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Convert Piety action Choose another player's closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be -5 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture)."}, {"title": "Sacred War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sacred War Piety action Declare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies."}, {"title": "Improve", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Improve Industry action Choose one: Infrastructure \u2014 choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time; when it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your province. Or Expand a Settlement one tier into an adjacent Territory (Village to Town, Town to City, City to Metropolis), adding a Ward."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Repair Industry action Choose a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Build Timer 2. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Holding tile from your Empire Tableau."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Build Industry action Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Holding with one complete line of its Mastery Chain under your control (and meet its other requirements) and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Holding in an available Ward slot; its effect activates immediately."}, {"title": "Charter", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Charter Industry action Charter a new Village \u2014 on in-province non-water, non-mountain Territory, range 4+ from any Settlement and range 2+ from Outlaw Country."}, {"title": "Sign Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sign Treaty Diplomacy action Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance."}, {"title": "Negotiate", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Negotiate Diplomacy action Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding)."}, {"title": "End Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "End Treaty Diplomacy action Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn't need to agree."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcomes", "url": "envoy-outcomes-ref.html", "text": "envoy outcomes condemned failed passed endorsed net influence resolve domain"}, {"title": "Peace Treaty", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Peace Treaty treaty Ends war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Trade Agreement", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Trade Agreement treaty Begin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires bordering + active Dirt Road."}, {"title": "Non-Aggression Pact", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Non-Aggression Pact treaty Neither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Military Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Military Alliance treaty Mutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy)."}, {"title": "Defensive Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Defensive Alliance treaty Mutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker."}, {"title": "Sovereign Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Sovereign Standing edict win Reach a Sovereign Standing (Domain value 10) in any Domain."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Monument edict win Have a Monument holding."}, {"title": "Wonder", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wonder edict win Improve Infrastructure via a Wonder."}, {"title": "Wealth", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wealth edict win Hold 50,000 gold in your Treasury for five consecutive turns."}, {"title": "Vassalize", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Vassalize edict win Vassalize a rival player (control their capital with no other settlements/armies under them)."}, {"title": "Living Saints", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Living Saints edict win Sustain Public Order 10 (Living Saints) for five consecutive turns (Pious Timer)."}, {"title": "Last Alliance Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Last Alliance Standing edict win Be the last alliance standing \u2014 the game-ending stop condition."}, {"title": "Economy Reference", "url": "economy-ref.html", "text": "upkeep costs pursuit army infrastructure tax trade 2000 gold (the envoy action; holding then costs per-turn upkeep by type) Per turn by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 1), Rising 200 (Build Timer 2), Established 300 (Build Timer 3), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 4); Natural 0 sum of each Army's cost (by Retinue type) - Upkeep -X modifiers Per-settlement (see INFRASTRUCTURE); Masonry removes Primitive, Trade Guild removes Developed, College of Engineering removes Sophisticated 2000 gold (Intercept Caravan / Foster Rebellion / Raze / Destabilize) 2000 gold (Build / Improve / Repair / Charter) Doubt 1 (Spread Truth / Send Missionaries / Tithe / Convert / Sacred War) None (Move / Declare War / Demand Tribute) None (Sign Treaty / Negotiate / End Treaty) Extort 2000 per settlement tier; reduce settlement by 1 tier; Sack Timer 2 500 gold per settlement tier per turn (collected in Winter) 100 x host's Craft X per active Trade Agreement"}, {"title": "Grassland", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Grassland terrain \u2014"}, {"title": "Wetlands", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Wetlands terrain Speed -1 per Territory moved through"}, {"title": "Tundra", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Tundra terrain gain Strained"}, {"title": "Mountains", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Mountains terrain Impassable"}, {"title": "Water", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Water terrain Must end move after moving over 1 Water Territory (must end on land)"}, {"title": "Forest", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Forest terrain Speed -1 per Territory moved through"}, {"title": "Hill", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Hill terrain Gains Seize the Initiative. Where Settlements can be chartered."}, {"title": "Terrain & Movement", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "terrain movement grassland wetland tundra mountain water forest roads bridge"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "bandits-ref.html", "text": "bandits outlaw country camp army growth cunning raze destabilize"}, {"title": "Timers, Influence & PO", "url": "systems-ref.html", "text": "timers influence public order modifiers faith doubt border tension"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "settlements-ref.html", "text": "settlements hamlet village town city metropolis tax muster wards reach"}, {"title": "Eras", "url": "eras-ref.html", "text": "eras founding ascension eminence zenith renown army cap"}, {"title": "Public Order Track", "url": "public-order-ref.html", "text": "public order faith doubt uprising living saints"}, {"title": "Domain Board", "url": "domain-board-ref.html", "text": "domain board standing indomitable grand vizier influence"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "seasons-ref.html", "text": "seasons winter spring summer fall"}, {"title": "Equipment", "url": "equipment-ref.html", "text": "equipment retinues weapons ranged shields armor stats"}, {"title": "Reference Tables", "url": "reference-tables.html", "text": "bandits timers influence gain trade rules build timers tier unlock standing effects"}, {"title": "Tactic Matrix", "url": "tactic-matrix-ref.html", "text": "tactic matrix scout ambush flank charge fighting defensive formation fall back initiative"}, {"title": "Escalation Campaign", "url": "escalation.html", "text": "escalation campaign combat battle mode overview"}, {"title": "Escalation Battle Rules", "url": "escalation-rules.html", "text": "escalation battle rules setup turn sequence skirmish walkthrough victory points dice"}, {"title": "Escalation Combat Pursuits", "url": "escalation-pursuits.html", "text": "escalation combat pursuits industry prowess piety cunning ranks mastery monument"}, {"title": "Combat Keywords", "url": "keywords-ref.html", "text": "keywords deadly cleave poison parry riposte"}, {"title": "Unbreakable", "url": "glossary.html#unbreakable", "text": "Unbreakable Skips the Break check entirely while Fatigued: never rolls, never takes break casualties. BUT still Routs if the morale target climbs to ROUT_THR+ from accumulated Fatigue. Stands fully immune, then collapses all at once \u2014 and because it stays full-size up to the Rout, it loses MORE soldiers when it finally breaks than a unit that bled down gradually."}, {"title": "Unshakable", "url": "glossary.html#unshakable", "text": "Unshakable Caps the morale target at CAP_THR permanently. Still TAKES every Break and Panic check each Skirmish (keeps bleeding casualties at a CAP_THR+ roll), but the target can never reach ROUT_THR, so it NEVER Routs. Bends and bleeds forever, never shatters. Makes the `shaking` stat (and the Abbey bonus) irrelevant \u2014 it's capped regardless."}, {"title": "Rally", "url": "glossary.html#rally", "text": "Rally Auto-passes the FIRST Break check it is ever required to take in a battle (no roll, no casualties, no Rout); every Break check after is normal. One free crisis, then mortal. The only one of the four that keeps `shaking` a live dial \u2014 so it's the one that synergizes with lowering KT base shaking and stacking Abbey +1."}, {"title": "Zealot", "url": "glossary.html#zealot", "text": "Zealot Locks the morale target at base `shaking`, ignoring ALL modifiers: Fatigue tokens don't raise it, shake bonuses (Abbey) don't lower it. Takes checks every Skirmish at that fixed number, never escalates, never Routs. A fixed wall whose strength is entirely its base stat. Unlike Unshakable (caps at 6), Zealot pins at base \u2014 which can be better or worse than 6 \u2014 and deliberately ignores Abbey synergy."}, {"title": "Steady", "url": "glossary.html#steady", "text": "Steady Initiative cannot be reduced by Tactics."}, {"title": "Unwieldy", "url": "glossary.html#unwieldy", "text": "Unwieldy Initiative cannot be improved by Tactics."}, {"title": "2H", "url": "glossary.html#2h", "text": "2H Cannot use a Shield: while a 2H weapon is Equipped, your Shield gives nothing that Skirmish (no Save bonus, Initiative or keywords)."}, {"title": "Deadly", "url": "glossary.html#deadly", "text": "Deadly On a Focused Strike: that strike's AP is increased by 5, and the defender may Parry or Recover only with a Focused roll."}, {"title": "Unstoppable", "url": "glossary.html#unstoppable", "text": "Unstoppable -2 to the defender's Parry roll, to a maximum of 10+)."}, {"title": "Cleave", "url": "glossary.html#cleave", "text": "Cleave On a Focused Strike: roll one extra Strike die at your modified to-Strike."}, {"title": "Poison", "url": "glossary.html#poison", "text": "Poison When the Defender receives a Strike and rolls a Focused Save, it fails; the resulting wound may only be Recovered with a Focused Recover."}, {"title": "Nimble", "url": "glossary.html#nimble", "text": "Nimble Gain +1 Initiative in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Drilled", "url": "glossary.html#drilled", "text": "Drilled Does not lose Endurance in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Destroy Shield", "url": "glossary.html#destroy-shield", "text": "Destroy Shield On a Focused Strike: the target loses its Shield attributes for the rest of the Battle."}, {"title": "Blunder", "url": "glossary.html#blunder", "text": "Blunder At Initiative -2, your to-Strike is set to 10+, before other negative modifiers."}, {"title": "One-Shot", "url": "glossary.html#one-shot", "text": "One-Shot Must be Equipped in the first Skirmish of a Battle, and can't be Equipped after it. Requires a Tiltyard."}, {"title": "Parry", "url": "glossary.html#parry", "text": "Parry Roll a D10 to attempt to Parry a Strike before an Armor Save. On a 8+ (Improved by Improved Parry), the Strike is Parried and has no further effect."}, {"title": "Riposte", "url": "glossary.html#riposte", "text": "Riposte If you Focused a Parry against a Melee Weapon's Strike, you Riposte: your opponent immediately takes a Strike from your melee weapon. You can Riposte a Riposte."}, {"title": "Awkward", "url": "glossary.html#awkward", "text": "Awkward While equipped with this weapon during a skirmish, you cannot Parry, and so cannot Riposte."}, {"title": "Recover", "url": "glossary.html#recover", "text": "Recover If a to-Save roll fails, roll a D10 & compare it to your Recover value: a result greater than or equal to your Recover value recovers the retinue. Recovered Strikes still count toward the Panic check threshold."}, {"title": "Enduring", "url": "glossary.html#enduring", "text": "Enduring Successfully Recovered Strikes don't count toward the Panic check threshold."}, {"title": "Serrated", "url": "glossary.html#serrated", "text": "Serrated A cumulative -2 penalty to the defender's Recover roll."}, {"title": "Planishing", "url": "glossary.html#planishing", "text": "Planishing A Focused Save succeeds, regardless of AP."}, {"title": "Fatigue Token", "url": "glossary.html#fatigue-token", "text": "Fatigue Token Each token reduces Morale  by 2 (uncapped); if your modified Morale is ever 11+, your army Routs. Tokens stack."}, {"title": "Shielded", "url": "glossary.html#shielded", "text": "Shielded A cumulative -1 penalty to the Strike roll (to a maximum of 10+). Sources: a shield's -1 to Strike."}, {"title": "Negate Planishing", "url": "glossary.html#negate-planishing", "text": "Negate Planishing Ignores Planishing: this weapon's AP can reduce the target's Save beyond 10+ (to auto-fail)."}, {"title": "Negate Riposte", "url": "glossary.html#negate-riposte", "text": "Negate Riposte The target's Parry can never Riposte this weapon's Strikes (a natural 10 Parry still cancels the Strike, but no counter-Strike follows)."}, {"title": "Dual Wield", "url": "glossary.html#dual-wield", "text": "Dual Wield A failed Strike is rerolled once; the rerolled Strike can be Focused. Dual Wield confers Two-Handed. You cannot reroll successful Strikes."}, {"title": "Immune [keyword]", "url": "glossary.html#immune-keyword", "text": "Immune [keyword] Cancels that keyword as it applies to you (e.g. Immune Unwieldy, Strain, Destroy Shield)."}, {"title": "AP", "url": "glossary.html#ap", "text": "AP Armor Penetration \u2014 a weapon's (negative) modifier to the defender's Save roll; the more negative, the harder to save."}, {"title": "Blocked", "url": "glossary.html#blocked", "text": "Blocked -1 Initiative in the first Skirmish (negated by Immune Blocked). Armies with Blocked cannot perform Move actions."}, {"title": "Strained", "url": "glossary.html#strained", "text": "Strained -1 Initiative every Skirmish (negated by Immune Strain). Does not gain Endurance in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Seize the Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#seize-the-initiative", "text": "Seize the Initiative Typically, the player who performed the Battle Action gains Seize the Initiative, but Terrain and the Ministry of Military Strategy can affect that. When a player gains Seize the Initiative, the player gains +1 Initiative in the first round of combat."}, {"title": "Attacker / Defender", "url": "glossary.html#attacker-defender", "text": "Attacker / Defender The Attacker performed the Move action that caused the Battle or Lay Siege; the other side is the Defender. Each Skirmish the Attacker declares equipment first; the Defender then responds."}, {"title": "Battle", "url": "glossary.html#battle", "text": "Battle One fight between two players, resolved as a series of Skirmishes until a side is wiped out, Routs, or Falls Back."}, {"title": "Skirmish", "url": "glossary.html#skirmish", "text": "Skirmish One round of a Battle, run through the numbered Battle steps; a Battle repeats Skirmishes until it ends."}, {"title": "Casualty", "url": "glossary.html#casualty", "text": "Casualty A retinue removed from the field \u2014 from an unsaved Strike or a failed Panic or Break check."}, {"title": "Field", "url": "glossary.html#field", "text": "Field Your retinues in play \u2014 front line (up to 10) plus reserve (up to 5). Casualties leave the field at once, lowering its count."}, {"title": "Endurance", "url": "glossary.html#endurance", "text": "Endurance A side's stamina. Each side that fights loses 1 per Skirmish; at 0 it becomes Fatigued."}, {"title": "Fatigued", "url": "glossary.html#fatigued", "text": "Fatigued A side at 0 Endurance. Each Skirmish its field takes a Break check, then it gains a Fatigue token."}, {"title": "Break check", "url": "glossary.html#break-check", "text": "Break check Taken by each Fatigued side's field every Skirmish, just before it gains its Fatigue token. Roll Morale (5 dice, modified by Fatigue tokens); failures are casualties, but a Break check never triggers a Panic check. Unbreakable auto-passes."}, {"title": "Panic check", "url": "glossary.html#panic-check", "text": "Panic check Taken at most once per Skirmish by a side that suffered more than 5 casualties in that Skirmish (Recovered Strikes count, unless Enduring), after both sides have Struck. Roll Morale (5 dice); Immune Panic auto-passes."}, {"title": "Morale", "url": "glossary.html#morale", "text": "Morale How steady a retinue is when tested (lower is steadier; see the retinue table). Break and Panic checks roll it: a D10 per retinue in the field, up to 5 dice, each must meet its modified value; failures are casualties. If the modified value is ever 11+, the army Routs."}, {"title": "Rout", "url": "glossary.html#rout", "text": "Rout The army breaks and leaves the Battle (you lose it). Whenever an army's modified Morale value reaches 11+ or more, it Routs automatically."}, {"title": "Fall Back", "url": "glossary.html#fall-back", "text": "Fall Back A controlled retreat that ends the Battle with at least one retinue left \u2014 a partial success."}, {"title": "Strike", "url": "glossary.html#strike", "text": "Strike A landed hit. Roll a D10, apply modifiers to the roll, and Strike on a result >= the to-Strike number. The target may then Parry, Save, and Recover."}, {"title": "to-Strike number", "url": "glossary.html#to-strike-number", "text": "to-Strike number The D10 result a retinue needs to Strike (see the retinue table; lower is better). Bonuses add to the roll; penalties and Fatigue tokens subtract."}, {"title": "Save", "url": "glossary.html#save", "text": "Save The defender's roll to avoid a casualty: roll a D10, add the weapon's AP (a negative) and the shield's Save bonus (a positive); the hit is saved on a result >= the armor value."}, {"title": "Natural roll", "url": "glossary.html#natural-roll", "text": "Natural roll The number on the die before any modifiers. Modifiers never change what counts as 'natural'."}, {"title": "Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#initiative", "text": "Initiative Decides who Strikes first each Skirmish (higher first). Runs -2 to +2 (Ministry can raise the maximum to +3). At -2 or lower you Blunder."}, {"title": "Tactic", "url": "glossary.html#tactic", "text": "Tactic A choice both players make secretly and reveal together each Skirmish; it can shift Initiative, Strike, and Save rolls."}, {"title": "Dual-equip", "url": "glossary.html#dual-equip", "text": "Dual-equip Carry two weapons at once (e.g. melee + ranged). Granted by the Tiltyard."}, {"title": "Edict", "url": "glossary.html#edict", "text": "Edict A scoring achievement / win path: reach a Sovereign Standing, complete a Monument, or fulfill a victory condition (Wonder, wealth, Vassalize, Living Saints, Last Standing)."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "glossary.html#monument", "text": "Monument A Domain's capstone Holding. Completing one scores its Edict and grants a powerful effect."}, {"title": "Faith X", "url": "glossary.html#faith-x", "text": "Faith X Gain X Faith: each Faith raises your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Doubt X", "url": "glossary.html#doubt-x", "text": "Doubt X Gain X Doubt: each Doubt lowers your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Extort X", "url": "glossary.html#extort-x", "text": "Extort X Take X from the stated source: the gold goes to you instead of its owner."}, {"title": "Recoup X", "url": "glossary.html#recoup-x", "text": "Recoup X Undo up to X of the cost you paid (refund gold, or remove Doubt gained)."}, {"title": "Speed X", "url": "glossary.html#speed-x", "text": "Speed X An Army's movement range in Territories per Move action. Base Speed value of an army is Speed 3"}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "glossary.html#influence", "text": "Influence The political currency of voting. Spend it to Support or Oppose Envoys. You gain it each turn from your Era, innate modifiers (trade partners, alliances, war), Holdings, and Infrastructure."}, {"title": "Influence X", "url": "glossary.html#influence-x", "text": "Influence X An automatic +X (or -X) to an Envoy's net Influence from a Holding, Infrastructure, or Faction."}, {"title": "Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#envoy", "text": "Envoy The currency of actions: send an Envoy to perform an action during the Envoy Phase. Council Envoys act on the voted Domain; Personal Envoys are sent by Era progression."}, {"title": "Vote", "url": "glossary.html#vote", "text": "Vote On each Envoy, every player except the sender, in clockwise order from the starting player, must Support, Oppose, or Abstain. No talking during a vote."}, {"title": "Support X", "url": "glossary.html#support-x", "text": "Support X Spend X Influence to increase an Envoy's net Influence."}, {"title": "Oppose X", "url": "glossary.html#oppose-x", "text": "Oppose X Spend X Influence to decrease an Envoy's net Influence."}, {"title": "Abstain", "url": "glossary.html#abstain", "text": "Abstain Decline to spend Influence on a vote."}, {"title": "Net Influence", "url": "glossary.html#net-influence", "text": "Net Influence The sum of an Envoy's starting Influence (1+ by Standing) and all Support, Oppose, and Influence X. The total sets the outcome: -3 or less Condemned, 0 or less Failed (gain Doubt +1), 1+ passes."}, {"title": "Endorsed", "url": "glossary.html#endorsed", "text": "Endorsed An Envoy that passes with 3+ net Influence, triggering its endorsed effect (and a Domain's Rising/Established/Sovereign endorsement)."}, {"title": "Condemned", "url": "glossary.html#condemned", "text": "Condemned An Envoy whose net Influence is -3 or less: it fails and you resolve that Domain's Condemn effect."}, {"title": "Council Phase", "url": "glossary.html#council-phase", "text": "Council Phase Before Personal Envoys, a brief Forum, then all players vote on a Domain with no talking (clockwise; Host breaks ties). Each then sends a free Council Envoy of that Domain. Council Envoys auto-Abstain and their net Influence cannot drop below 1."}, {"title": "Council Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#council-envoy", "text": "Council Envoy A free Envoy resolved in the Council Phase on the voted Domain; auto-Abstained, net Influence floored at 1."}, {"title": "Personal Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#personal-envoy", "text": "Personal Envoy An Envoy you send in the Envoy Phase to perform an action; count and reach scale with Era."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcome", "url": "glossary.html#envoy-outcome", "text": "Envoy Outcome How a Sent Envoy resolves, by Net Influence: Condemned (<= -3), Failed (-3 < Net <= 0, gain Doubt 1), Passed (>= 1), Endorsed (>= 3). The per-domain effect at each band is given by the Envoy Outcome Table; an action's own endorsed bonus overrides the domain default."}, {"title": "Charter", "url": "glossary.html#charter", "text": "Charter Found a new Settlement (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "glossary.html#muster", "text": "Muster Raise a new Army or Reinforce an existing one near a Muster Field; Retinues arrive each turn over a Muster Timer (Prowess action)."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "glossary.html#build", "text": "Build Build a Holding, spending its purchase cost and a Settlement ward (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Improve", "url": "glossary.html#improve", "text": "Improve Construct Infrastructure or Expand a Settlement one tier (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "glossary.html#repair", "text": "Repair Restore damaged Infrastructure or Settlements (Industry)."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "glossary.html#move", "text": "Move Advance an Army up to its Speed in Territories (Prowess)."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "glossary.html#demand-tribute", "text": "Demand Tribute Coerce gold or concessions from another player (Prowess)."}, {"title": "Diplomacy", "url": "glossary.html#diplomacy", "text": "Diplomacy Free Envoy actions for forming and ending Treaties and Trade Agreements; resolved before Domain Envoys."}, {"title": "Treaty", "url": "glossary.html#treaty", "text": "Treaty A standing agreement between players (e.g. Trade Agreement, Non-Aggression, Alliance) signed via Diplomacy."}, {"title": "Alliance", "url": "glossary.html#alliance", "text": "Alliance A Treaty binding players to mutual support; Military and Defensive Alliances unlock by Era."}, {"title": "Vassal", "url": "glossary.html#vassal", "text": "Vassal A player subordinated via Vassalization: their chartered settlements return to them, they mirror the Suzerain's Treaties, count as allied to the Suzerain, and cannot perform or be targeted by Diplomacy actions."}, {"title": "Suzerain", "url": "glossary.html#suzerain", "text": "Suzerain The player who has Vassalized another; the vassal mirrors their Treaties."}, {"title": "Renown", "url": "glossary.html#renown", "text": "Renown The shared progress track. Gain 1 per Rest Phase; thresholds raise your Era (Ascension 8, Eminence 18, Zenith 30)."}, {"title": "Domain", "url": "glossary.html#domain", "text": "Domain One of the four identities \u2014 Industry, Prowess, Cunning, Piety \u2014 raised by spending Domain points. Values 3/6/10 = Rising/Established/Sovereign Standing."}, {"title": "Domain Point", "url": "glossary.html#domain-point", "text": "Domain Point Gain 1 per Rest Phase; spend to raise a Domain value by 1."}, {"title": "Standing", "url": "glossary.html#standing", "text": "Standing Your tier in a Domain: Untested, Rising (3), Established (6), Sovereign (10). Sets max Influence per vote (1/2/3/4) and unlocks Domain effects."}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "glossary.html#public-order", "text": "Public Order A track from -5 to 10, adjusted each turn by Faith minus Doubt; its band applies cumulative effects (see the Public Order table)."}, {"title": "Reach", "url": "glossary.html#reach", "text": "Reach How far a Settlement projects control, in Territories (by tier). Calculated like Range X"}, {"title": "Bandit", "url": "glossary.html#bandit", "text": "Bandit Neutral hostile force; Bandit Camps spawn in Outlaw Country and on low Public Order."}, {"title": "Outlaw Country", "url": "glossary.html#outlaw-country", "text": "Outlaw Country Uncontrollable territories in your starting region where Bandit Camps spawn, starting at 3 and expanding if there is no room to place new Bandit Camps."}, {"title": "Siege", "url": "glossary.html#siege", "text": "Siege Sieging a Settlement with an Army to capture it; does not increment in Winter."}, {"title": "Border", "url": "glossary.html#border", "text": "Border Your Settlement's Reach is Range 1 or within Reach of another Player's Reach."}, {"title": "Province", "url": "glossary.html#province", "text": "Province The collection of Contested Territory and Controlled Territory by your Settlement's Reach."}, {"title": "Region", "url": "glossary.html#region", "text": "Region A collection of Territories of the same Type."}, {"title": "Realm", "url": "glossary.html#realm", "text": "Realm The total collection of Regions."}, {"title": "Territory", "url": "glossary.html#territory", "text": "Territory 1 Hex."}, {"title": "Contested", "url": "glossary.html#contested", "text": "Contested Territory that is within Reach of more than one player's settlement(s). Considered Controlled by all Players that have a Settlement within Reach."}, {"title": "Controlled", "url": "glossary.html#controlled", "text": "Controlled Territory that is within Reach of a single Player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Uncontrolled", "url": "glossary.html#uncontrolled", "text": "Uncontrolled Territory that is not within Reach of any Player Settlement."}, {"title": "Adjacent", "url": "glossary.html#adjacent", "text": "Adjacent Range 1."}, {"title": "Next to", "url": "glossary.html#next-to", "text": "Next to Range 2."}, {"title": "Within", "url": "glossary.html#within", "text": "Within Range 0."}, {"title": "Range X", "url": "glossary.html#range-x", "text": "Range X The amount of Territories you must move in order to get from your current position to the specific Territory."}, {"title": "Reach X", "url": "glossary.html#reach-x", "text": "Reach X The Range X characteristic which determines what Territories you Control and are in your Province."}, {"title": "Host", "url": "glossary.html#host", "text": "Host Holds the Host Card; the starting player is the player directly clockwise from the Host, including in Spring. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (there is no Host in Spring). The Host collects and distributes Trade Income, resolves Bandit Mechanics, and breaks ties (Council vote, bandit targeting, and any tie not otherwise resolved)."}, {"title": "Send an Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#send-an-envoy", "text": "Send an Envoy Declare a Domain, spend 1 Envoy."}, {"title": "Perform", "url": "glossary.html#perform", "text": "Perform When you Perform an action, immediately do the description of the action. Pay the action's normal Cost."}, {"title": "Resolve", "url": "glossary.html#resolve", "text": "Resolve Attempt to Perform an action."}, {"title": "Cost / Pay", "url": "glossary.html#cost-pay", "text": "Cost / Pay Cost to perform an action, usually in Gold or Doubt."}, {"title": "Fail", "url": "glossary.html#fail", "text": "Fail An unsuccessful to Hit or to Save."}, {"title": "Failed", "url": "glossary.html#failed", "text": "Failed Net Influence 0 or less."}, {"title": "Passed", "url": "glossary.html#passed", "text": "Passed Net Influence 1 or more."}, {"title": "Focused", "url": "glossary.html#focused", "text": "Focused A natural 10, before modifiers."}, {"title": "Sally Forth", "url": "glossary.html#sally-forth", "text": "Sally Forth While a settlement you control is besieged and you have an army inside it, you may Sally Forth: Battle in the Battle Phase without performing an action."}, {"title": "War Weariness", "url": "glossary.html#war-weariness", "text": "War Weariness gain Doubt 1 for each consecutive Battle you lose in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Settlement Ward", "url": "glossary.html#settlement-ward", "text": "Settlement Ward A slot in a Settlement that holds one Holding; a Settlement has one Ward per tier (a Hamlet has 3 Husbandry Wards)."}, {"title": "Mastery Chain X", "url": "glossary.html#mastery-chain-x", "text": "Mastery Chain X While this Holding occupies the same Settlement Ward as X (the Raw Material or Holding named on its tile), it uses no ward of its own \u2014 the two share one ward. Placed anywhere else, it fills a ward normally. (Core Principle 14.) Note: Two Holdings that chain from the same Holding cannot share a Ward with each other."}, {"title": "Natural", "url": "glossary.html#natural", "text": "Natural Natural Holdings do not cost Upkeep & can be used in Hamlets."}, {"title": "Upkeep", "url": "glossary.html#upkeep", "text": "Upkeep Gold you pay each Empire Phase for Armies, Holdings and Infrastructure. Holding upkeep is by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 1), Rising 200 (Build Timer 2), Established 300 (Build Timer 3), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 4); Natural 0; a Holding pays no upkeep while its Build Timer is running. Army upkeep = the sum of each Army's cost (by Retinue type) \u2212 Upkeep modifiers."}, {"title": "Craft", "url": "glossary.html#craft", "text": "Craft Craft Holdings count toward how much income your Trade Agreements generate \u2014 any effect that grants Craft +X. For each active Trade Agreement, both players gain 100 \u00d7 the Host's Craft X."}, {"title": "Mastery Chain", "url": "glossary.html#mastery-chain", "text": "Mastery Chain A Holding's Mastery Chain is the line of Holdings it builds from, usually running from a Raw Material up to a Monument. You may start building a Holding only while you control one complete line of its Mastery Chain, anywhere in your empire; this is checked only when you start it. A Holding placed in the same Settlement Ward as its immediate parent shares that Ward, and the chain can continue upward the same way. Each Holding carries at most one descendant in its Ward. (Core Principle 14.)"}, {"title": "Pursuit", "url": "glossary.html#pursuit", "text": "Pursuit An object that is placed into a Settlement Ward or onto a Root Holding as a result of a Build action, giving effects which affect your Empire in many ways."}, {"title": "Retinue", "url": "glossary.html#retinue", "text": "Retinue A single unit within an Army, represented by a single die roll for Strikes, Saves, etc."}, {"title": "At War", "url": "glossary.html#at-war", "text": "At War Cannot trade; can be the target of Siege, Battle, & Pillage actions from players At War with this player."}, {"title": "Equipped", "url": "glossary.html#equipped", "text": "Equipped The weapon chosen for the Skirmish."}, {"title": "Build Timer", "url": "glossary.html#build-timer", "text": "Build Timer Turns until an infrastructure/build completes and becomes Active."}, {"title": "Repair Timer", "url": "glossary.html#repair-timer", "text": "Repair Timer Turns until a Damaged piece is repaired and its effects return."}, {"title": "Truce Timer", "url": "glossary.html#truce-timer", "text": "Truce Timer Turns remaining until a Truce expires (and related diplomacy restrictions end)."}, {"title": "Siege Timer", "url": "glossary.html#siege-timer", "text": "Siege Timer Turns remaining until a Siege resolves."}, {"title": "Muster Timer", "url": "glossary.html#muster-timer", "text": "Muster Timer Turns remaining in a Muster; each turn it counts down, the Army gains Retinues up to the combined muster limit."}, {"title": "Sack Timer", "url": "glossary.html#sack-timer", "text": "Sack Timer Cooldown before the same force may Lay Siege again (per Sack rules)."}, {"title": "Capture Timer", "url": "glossary.html#capture-timer", "text": "Capture Timer Turns until a Captured Settlement becomes Controlled by the Player with the Capture Timer and applies the listed capture effects."}, {"title": "Convert Timer", "url": "glossary.html#convert-timer", "text": "Convert Timer Turns until a Convert attempt resolves (or fails early if conditions change)."}, {"title": "Crude", "url": "glossary.html#crude", "text": "Crude Crude equipment tier. Weapons: Farm Tools, Cudgel, Pitchfork; Ranged: Hunting Bow; Armor: Gambeson; Shield: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Crude Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#crude-weapons", "text": "Crude Weapons Crude-tier weapons: Farm Tools, Cudgel, Pitchfork, Hunting Bow."}, {"title": "Crude Armor", "url": "glossary.html#crude-armor", "text": "Crude Armor Crude-tier armor: Gambeson. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry."}, {"title": "Crude Shields", "url": "glossary.html#crude-shields", "text": "Crude Shields Crude-tier shields: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry."}, {"title": "Cast", "url": "glossary.html#cast", "text": "Cast Cast equipment tier. Weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spears; Ranged: Longbow; Armor: Leather; Shield: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery (armor & shield), Furnace (weapons)."}, {"title": "Cast Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#cast-weapons", "text": "Cast Weapons Cast-tier weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spears, Longbow. Unlocked by: Furnace."}, {"title": "Cast Armor", "url": "glossary.html#cast-armor", "text": "Cast Armor Cast-tier armor: Leather. Unlocked by: Tannery."}, {"title": "Cast Shields", "url": "glossary.html#cast-shields", "text": "Cast Shields Cast-tier shields: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Tannery."}, {"title": "Wrought", "url": "glossary.html#wrought", "text": "Wrought Wrought equipment tier. Weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear; Ranged: Javelin; Armor: Chainmail; Shield: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Blacksmith (weapons), Armory (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Wrought Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#wrought-weapons", "text": "Wrought Weapons Wrought-tier weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear, Javelin. Unlocked by: Blacksmith."}, {"title": "Wrought Armor", "url": "glossary.html#wrought-armor", "text": "Wrought Armor Wrought-tier armor: Chainmail. Unlocked by: Armory."}, {"title": "Wrought Shields", "url": "glossary.html#wrought-shields", "text": "Wrought Shields Wrought-tier shields: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Armory."}, {"title": "Forged", "url": "glossary.html#forged", "text": "Forged Forged equipment tier. Weapons: Morningstar, Bastard Sword, 2HBastard, War Hammer, Lance; Ranged: Crossbow; Armor: Full Plate; Shield: Tower Shield. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry (armor & shield), Forge (all)."}, {"title": "Forged Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#forged-weapons", "text": "Forged Weapons Forged-tier weapons: Morningstar, Bastard Sword, 2HBastard, War Hammer, Lance, Crossbow. Unlocked by: Forge."}, {"title": "Forged Armor", "url": "glossary.html#forged-armor", "text": "Forged Armor Forged-tier armor: Full Plate. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry, Forge."}, {"title": "Forged Shields", "url": "glossary.html#forged-shields", "text": "Forged Shields Forged-tier shields: Tower Shield. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry, Forge."}, {"title": "Tempered", "url": "glossary.html#tempered", "text": "Tempered Tempered equipment tier. Weapons: Estoc, Poleaxe; Ranged: Pilum; Armor: Gothic Plate; Shield: Heater Shield."}, {"title": "Tempered Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#tempered-weapons", "text": "Tempered Weapons Tempered-tier weapons: Estoc, Poleaxe, Pilum."}, {"title": "Tempered Armor", "url": "glossary.html#tempered-armor", "text": "Tempered Armor Tempered-tier armor: Gothic Plate."}, {"title": "Tempered Shields", "url": "glossary.html#tempered-shields", "text": "Tempered Shields Tempered-tier shields: Heater Shield."}, {"title": "Gunpowder", "url": "glossary.html#gunpowder", "text": "Gunpowder Gunpowder equipment: Arquebus. Unlocked by: Artillery Park, Fletchery."}, {"title": "Ranged Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#ranged-weapons", "text": "Ranged Weapons Ranged weapons: Hunting Bow (Crude), Longbow (Cast), Javelin (Wrought), Crossbow (Forged), Pilum (Tempered), Arquebus (Gunpowder). Unlocked by: Fletchery."}, {"title": "Root", "url": "glossary.html#root", "text": "Root A Holding with no Mastery Chain requirement: you may start it without controlling a parent. If it is Efficient with a Holding, it may still share that Holding's Settlement Ward."}, {"title": "Map Generator", "url": "maps.html", "text": "map generator procedural board terrain hex seed rivers lakes resources start map"}, {"title": "Board Emulator", "url": "board.html", "text": "settlement board emulator pursuits wards infrastructure army public order renown domains"}, {"title": "The World of Vaelohk", "url": "lore.html", "text": "lore world vaelohk premise draggath fracture peoples"}, {"title": "The Map", "url": "lore-map.html", "text": "map vaelohk sea corners centre regions places geography duke unclaimed"}, {"title": "The Fifteen", "url": "lore-cultures.html", "text": "cultures fifteen Trusteki Ithiss Prezish Voldrastel Lenavorites Madekites Belvareth Shassolin Kraghs Vorghith Drakteni Cailendroffs Sarkopekt Astravantheliad Ossensteins"}, {"title": "The Timeline", "url": "lore-ages.html", "text": "timeline ages fracture plenty tetramorph doubt renown chronicle"}, {"title": "The Age of Darkness", "url": "lore-darkness.html", "text": "age of darkness old gods foundings draggath trusti clypso cailen"}];const q=document.getElementById('q'),box=document.getElementById('results');let sel=-1,cur=[];
q.addEventListener('input',()=>{const v=q.value.toLowerCase().trim();sel=-1;if(v.length<2){box.style.display='none';return;}
cur=IDX.map(d=>{const t=d.title.toLowerCase(),x=d.text.toLowerCase();let s=0;if(t===v)s=100;else if(t.startsWith(v))s=60;else if(t.includes(v))s=40;else if(x.includes(v))s=15;return{d,s};}).filter(o=>o.s>0).sort((a,b)=>b.s-a.s).slice(0,14);
if(!cur.length){box.innerHTML='<a><span class=s>No matches</span></a>';box.style.display='block';return;}
box.innerHTML=cur.map((o,i)=>`<a href="${o.d.url}" data-i="${i}"><span class="t">${o.d.title}</span> <span class="s">${o.d.text.slice(0,80).replace(/</g,'&lt;')}…</span></a>`).join('');box.style.display='block';});
q.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{const a=box.querySelectorAll('a');if(e.key==='ArrowDown')sel=Math.min(sel+1,a.length-1);else if(e.key==='ArrowUp')sel=Math.max(sel-1,0);else if(e.key==='Enter'&&cur.length){location.href=cur[Math.max(sel,0)].d.url;return;}else return;a.forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('sel',i===sel));e.preventDefault();});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target!==q)box.style.display='none';});